<title>POLAND: POLISH NEW CAR SALES UP 32 PCT IN FIRST QUARTER.</title>
<headline>POLISH NEW CAR SALES UP 32 PCT IN FIRST QUARTER.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>New car sales in Poland grew in</p>
<p>the first quarter of this year by 32.11 percent against the</p>
<p>same period of last year to 130,383 units, an independent car</p>
<p>market monitoring agency, Samar, said on Thursday in a report.</p>
<p>Samar said sales of commercial vehicles rose 23 percent to</p>
<p>10,733 over the same period.</p>
<p>Fiat topped the list of passenger car makers with</p>
<p>44,162 units sold and a 33.9 percent market share. It was the</p>
<p>only maker in the top five which saw its market share shrink.</p>
<p>In the first quarter of 1996 Fiat had a 40.2 percent share</p>
<p>of the Polish market.</p>
